;;; tur/typeclass-drop -- Drop typeclass for releasing an owned value.
;;;
;;; Auto-loaded (like typeclass-clone.tur) so a module can declare
;;; (definstance Drop [...] ...) without importing typeclass.tur.
;;;
;;; A type implements Drop when it OWNS a resource that must be released when the
;;; value dies -- a refcounted handle (decrement), a unique heap pointer (free),
;;; a nested owning aggregate (walk).  The closure drop-glue
;;; (docs/archive/closure-drop-glue-plan.md, Model R) dispatches through a
;;; capture's Drop instance to release it when the capturing env is freed, so an
;;; owned value captured into an escaping closure no longer leaks.
;;;
;;; Drop composes with Clone: a Drop type that is ALSO Clone (e.g. a refcounted
;;; String) is RETAINed (via clone) when captured and released (via drop) when the
;;; env dies, so the retain/release balances regardless of aliasing.  A Drop type
;;; that is NOT Clone is move-only: capturing it consumes the source (a second
;;; use is a compile-time use-after-move), so the env is its sole owner.
;;;
;;; Since: v2 (Model R)
;;
;;; Drop -- values that own a resource to release when the value dies.
;;;
;;; Parameters:
;;;   a -- the owning type
;;;
;;; Methods:
;;;   drop -- release what `x` owns -- decrement a refcount, free a unique
;;;           pointer, walk a nested owner.  The closure drop-glue calls it
;;;           when a capturing env is freed; `x` is not used afterwards.
;;;
;;; Implement Drop only for a type that really owns something.  Pair it with
;;; Clone for a shareable (refcounted) type; leave Clone off to make the type
;;; move-only.
;;;
;;; Since: v2 (Model R)
(defclass Drop [a] (drop [x] : void))
